<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 6 November, from 447 to 1962.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/walls-of-constantinople" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/walls-of-constantinople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">447 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,579 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake destroys large parts of the Walls of Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A powerful earthquake destroyed large parts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walls-of-constantinople">Walls of Constantinople</a>, including 57 towers. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila the Hun</a> threatening from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-ii">Theodosius II</a> had them restored, reportedly in a record 60 days, using the city's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a>-racing factions.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walls-of-constantinople">Walls of Constantinople</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/963">963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,063 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Otto I convenes a synod in Rome to depose Pope John XII</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under the authority of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a>, a possibly uncanonical synod met in Saint Peter's Basilica to depose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-john-xii">Pope John XII</a>, who had crowned Otto emperor in 962, for armed rebellion against him. The synod sat until 4 December.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-john-xii">Pope John XII</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-peters-basilica">St. Peter's Basilica</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1217">1217 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">809 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry III issues the Charter of the Forest</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The young King Henry III, under the regency of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-marshal-1st-earl-of-pembroke">William Marshal, 1st Earl of Pembroke</a>, issued the Charter of the Forest at Old St Paul's Cathedral, restoring free men's rights of access to the royal forest. It complemented <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magna-carta">Magna Carta</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1860">1860 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">166 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Abraham Lincoln is elected president</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a> won the presidency with under 40 per cent of the popular vote, carrying only northern states. His victory prompted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a> to secede within weeks, followed by six more states.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1869">1869 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">157 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rutgers and Princeton play the first college football game</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rutgers beat Princeton 6-4 in New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a>, in the first intercollegiate football match. The rules resembled soccer more than modern American football.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1913">1913 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">113 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gandhi is arrested leading a march of Indian miners</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Gandhi</a> was arrested at Palmford while leading over 2,000 striking Indian workers across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> border in defiance of discriminatory laws. The campaign won concessions in 1914.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1917">1917 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Canadian troops capture Passchendaele</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Canadian forces took the ruined village of Passchendaele, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-passchendaele">Third Battle of Ypres</a>. The British-led offensive had gained a few miles of Flemish mud at a cost of hundreds of thousands of casualties.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1962">1962 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The UN General Assembly calls for sanctions on South Africa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Resolution 1761 condemned apartheid and urged member states to break diplomatic ties and boycott South African trade. It also set up a special committee against apartheid.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 6 November <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-spain"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-ii-of-spain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles II of Spain</span><span class="tp">1661–1700</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adolphe-sax"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/adolphe-sax.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Adolphe Sax</span><span class="tp">1814–1894</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 6 November <span class="n">1</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edwin-barclay"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edwin-barclay.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edwin Barclay</span><span class="tp">1882–1955</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
